build: 2026-06-30 v10.76.56 (Visual rings concentric from the FIRST frame)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: Fix: "Die Visual-Kreise sind am Anfang viel, bis man das Handy dreht — sie sollen immer
  concentrisch sein." Root cause: the renderer's aspect ratio was set ONLY when the drawable
  size changed (rotation). On launch that callback fires late / with a stale size, so the first
  frames rendered with aspect = 1 — on a tall phone that stretches the radial metric into
  ellipses, so the rings looked non-concentric (busy/elliptical) until a rotation forced a
  resize. Now the aspect is recomputed from the LIVE drawable size every frame, so the rings are
  perfectly concentric from the very first frame — no rotation needed.
  Test 10.76.56: open the immersive visual fresh (no rotating) — rings should be round/concentric
  immediately. (Pulse note: this log was again a flickering contact — finger kept lifting, 6 fps —
  so it didn't lock; that's contact, not the visual fix.)
